// REJECTS: Unexpected token
//
// Section imports come FIRST, before any element in the section. This puts the import
// after the Diagram it would have applied to.
//
// The rule is uninteresting until you notice why it is not enforceable by the walker: the
// import list scopes path resolution for everything after it, so "imports anywhere" is not
// just untidy, it makes resolution order-dependent within a section. A rewrite that
// collects imports wherever it finds them and applies them section-wide accepts this file
// AND changes the meaning of a legal one, because a path that resolved via the imports at
// the top now also resolves via imports declared below it.
###Diagram
Diagram fixture::neg::LateImport
{
   classView v1
   {
      class: fixture::neg::Person;
      position: (1.0,2.0);
      rectangle: (10.0,20.0);
   }
}

import fixture::neg::*;
